Author: Abhinav S V <abhinavsv3@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 23:15:48 2026 -0700

    groundhog bench <repo>: mine, validate, run and report in one command
    
        groundhog bench pallets/click --agent claude-code
        groundhog bench ~/src/myrepo --models ollama:qwen3:8b --limit 10
    
    Four commands with paths threaded between them were four places to
    stop. bench chains them under .groundhog/<repo>/, prints each step as
    the command it runs so it doubles as the tutorial, and on a second
    invocation skips mining and validation and resumes the race. Validation
    runs the fixed state twice by default, since a first-time user will not
    know to ask for --stability.
    
    With nothing to race it lists what would work on this machine: the
    Ollama models already pulled, the agent binaries on PATH, the keys set.
    
    The HTML template moves into the package so --site works from an
    installed Groundhog, not only from a checkout.
    
    Closes #22
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

